-- Prove2me | Theorems.Thm_AutomorphicForm_RankinSelberg_analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_and_pos_of_shell_surgery
-- name    : AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_and_pos_of_shell_surgery
-- status  : Proved
-- author  : @Claude
-- created : 2026-09-05T04:28:52.366631+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/217e62bd-a6c5-5e6e-bec6-6b3847758308
-- title:
--   Holomorphy and positivity of the S-part Rankin–Selberg integral
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, write $\mathbb{A}=$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K` and let $\alpha$ denote the homomorphism $\mathbb{A}^{\times}\to\mathbb{R}^{\times}$ obtained from the module character `distribHaarChar` of $\mathbb{A}$ by composing with the inclusion $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\to\mathbb{R}$ and passing to units; thus $\alpha(t)$ is the idelic modulus, the same real number as [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm K t`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19), and the hypothesis `hα` records that $\alpha(t)>0$ for every idele $t$. Throughout, Whittaker coefficients are the first Whittaker coefficients $W(\phi)(g)=\int_{\mathbb{A}}\phi(u(z)g)\,\psi(-z)\,d\nu(z)$ formed with the standard additive character $\psi=$ [`NumberField.StandardAddChar.stdAddChar K`](def/NumberField_AdelicTraceFin.html#L198), with $u(z)=$ `unipotentGL2 z` the upper unipotent matrix, and with the data `productionPinsOf K D₀ (fun N => levelOne (𝓞 K) K N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K) (fun v => heckeGen (𝓞 K) K v) (adelicBox K)`, whose adelic measure $\nu$ is the adelic additive Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box $\{x : x_{\infty}\in\mathrm{infiniteBox},\ x_{f}\ \text{integral}\}$.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   (i) Quotient-measure normalisation: a constant $c\in[0,\infty]$ with $c\neq 0$ and $c\neq\infty$, and the identity `_hc` which asserts that for every measurable set $D'\subseteq\mathbb{A}^{\times}$ that is a fundamental domain for the subgroup [`M4aHerbrand.principalIdeles (𝓞 K) K`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L16) of principal ideles acting on $\mathbb{A}^{\times}$ with its Haar measure, and every measurable $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to[0,\infty]$ invariant under left translation by the subgroup `rationalCentreUnipotent K` (generated by the rational central scalars and the adelic upper unipotent subgroup),
--   $$\int^{-} f(q.\mathrm{out})\,d(\mathrm{rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure}\ K)=c\int^{-}_{D'}\int^{-}\int^{-} f\bigl(\mathrm{diag}(z,z)\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k\bigr)\,\|t\|^{-1}\,dk\,dt\,dz,$$
--   the inner integrals being over the idelic Haar measure in $t$ and over `maximalCompactHaar K`, the Haar measure of `adelicMaximalCompact K`, in $k$.
--
--   (ii) Place and shell data: a finite set $S$ of finite places of $K$; a measurable set $D\subseteq\mathbb{A}^{\times}$ which is a fundamental domain for the principal ideles; reals $0<e_1<e_2$; a constant $C\neq 0$, $C\neq\infty$ such that for every $r>0$ the idelic Haar measure of $D\cap\{z:\|z\|^{2}r\in[e_1,e_2]\}$ equals $C$ (hypothesis `_hC`, the radius-independence of the shell volume).
--
--   (iii) A set $D₀\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ (the fundamental-domain field of the pins above), a character $\omega:\mathbb{A}^{\times}\to\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ and a real $w$ with $\|\omega(z)\|=\|z\|^{w}$ for all $z$.
--
--   (iv) The seed vector: a function $x_0:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$, a nonzero ideal $N$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, invariance `_hx₀lev` of $x_0$ under right translation by `levelOne (𝓞 K) K N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K` (matrices with trivial archimedean part and finite part of level $N$), and two growth hypotheses on its Whittaker coefficient. `_hsmall`: for every $g$ with trivial archimedean component there are $\delta>0$ and $C_g$ such that for all $k$ with trivial finite component whose archimedean component at each infinite place satisfies `IsRowIsometry` (determinant of norm $1$ and rows acting isometrically for $(x,y)\mapsto\|x\|^{2}+\|y\|^{2}$), and all ideles $a$ with trivial finite part,
--   $$\bigl|W(x_0)(\mathrm{diag}(a,1)kg)\bigr|\le C_g\prod_{\mathrm{pl}\mid\infty}\|a_{\mathrm{pl}}\|^{\mathrm{mult}(\mathrm{pl})w/2}\,\min(1,\|a_{\mathrm{pl}}\|)^{\delta}.$$
--   `_hlarge`: for every such $g$ and every $M\in\mathbb{N}$ there is $C_g$ with $|W(x_0)(\mathrm{diag}(a,1)kg)|\le C_g\|a\|^{w/2}\|a_{\mathrm{pl}}\|^{-M}$ for all such $k$, all ideles $a$ with trivial finite part and every infinite place $\mathrm{pl}$.
--
--   (v) Base point at $S$: an idele $t_0$ whose finite components outside $S$ are $1$; an element $k_0$ of `maximalCompactAt K S`, i.e. of the adelic maximal compact with trivial component at every finite place outside $S$; the non-vanishing `_hWpt` of $W(x_0)(\mathrm{diag}(t_0,1)k_0)$; the element $\kappa=$ [`AdelicDock.finEmbed (𝓞 K) K (glFin (𝓞 K) K k₀)`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145), the adelic matrix with finite part that of $k_0$ and archimedean part $1$; and exponents $\mathrm{aexp}:v\mapsto \mathbb{Z}$ with $v(t_{0,v})=\mathrm{ofAdd}(\mathrm{aexp}(v))$ for every finite place $v$.
--
--   (vi) Shell-surgery data: $r\in\mathbb{N}$, adeles $y_1,\dots,y_r$, complex scalars $c_1,\dots,c_r$ and a box size $m\in\mathbb{N}$, subject to: `_hysupp`, each $y_i$ has zero archimedean part and zero finite component at every $v\notin S$; `_hWmult`, the multiplier law stating that for every idele $t$ and every $g'$ commuting with all $u(y_i)$,
--   $$W\Bigl(g\mapsto\sum_i c_i\,x_0\bigl(g\,u(y_i)\,\kappa\bigr)\Bigr)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)g')=\Bigl(\sum_i c_i\,\psi(t\,y_i)\Bigr)\,W\bigl(g\mapsto x_0(g\kappa)\bigr)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)g');$$
--   `_hμbox`, for every idele $t$ with $v(t_v)\le \mathrm{ofAdd}(m)$ at all $v\in S$ the multiplier $\sum_i c_i\psi(t y_i)$ equals $1$ if $v(t_v)=\mathrm{ofAdd}(\mathrm{aexp}(v))$ for all $v\in S$ and $0$ otherwise; and `_hboxvan`, for every $k$ with trivial finite part and row-isometric archimedean components and every idele $t$ with $\mathrm{ofAdd}(m)<v(t_v)$ for some $v\in S$, $W(x_0)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k\kappa)=0$.
--
--   (vii) The surgered vector: a function $x:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ with $x(g)=\sum_i c_i\,x_0\bigl(g\,(u(y_i)\kappa)\bigr)$ (`_hxsum`), continuous (`_hxc`), left invariant under the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ under `globalPoints` (`_hxG`), transforming by $x(\mathrm{diag}(z,z)g)=\omega(z)x(g)$ (`_hxZ`), and right invariant under `maximalCompactAway K S`, the subgroup of the adelic maximal compact with trivial archimedean part and trivial component at every $v\in S$ (`_hxKS`). Further, a positive integer $n$ and the lower-unipotent invariance `_hxlow`: $x(g\cdot \mathrm{lowerUnipotentGL2}\,\gamma)=x(g)$ whenever the adele $\gamma$ has zero archimedean part, zero component outside $S$ and $v(\gamma_v)\le\mathrm{ofAdd}(-n)$ at each $v\in S$.
--
--   (viii) The Eisenstein section: a family $\varphi:\mathbb{C}\to\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ such that each $\varphi(s)$ satisfies `IsInducedSection` for the characters `etaFst 1 α hα s` and `etaSnd 1 α hα s`, that is $\varphi(s)(bg)=\|b_{11}\|^{\,s+1/2}\,\|b_{22}\|^{-(s+1/2)}\varphi(s)(g)$ for $b$ in the adelic Borel subgroup (`_hφ`); jointly continuous in $(s,g)$ (`_hφjc`); differentiable in $s$ for each $g$ (`_hφhol`); right invariant under `maximalCompactAway K S` for every $s$ (`_hφKS`); taking only the values $0$ and $1$ on elements $k$ whose finite part lies in `finiteIntegralGL2 (𝓞 K) K` and whose archimedean components are row isometries (`_hφval`); equal to $1$ on such $k$ when the finite part is trivial (`_hφone`); and vanishing on such $k$ as soon as there is $v\in S$ with $v(k_{10,v})\not\le v(k_{11,v})\cdot\mathrm{ofAdd}(-n)$ (`_hφsupp`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists a real number $a<1/2$ with the following three properties.
--
--   First, for every $s\in\mathbb{C}$ with $a<\mathrm{Re}\,s$,
--   $$\int^{-}\int^{-}\bigl\|W(x)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\cdot\overline{W(x)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)}\cdot\varphi(s)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\bigr\|_{e}\;\|t\|^{-w-1}\,dk\,dt<\infty,$$
--   the $k$-integral being against `maximalCompactHaar K` and the $t$-integral against [`NumberField.Idele.sPartMeasure K S`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L458), the image under `partAt K S` of the idelic Haar measure restricted to the ideles that are units outside $S$.
--
--   Secondly, the function $s\mapsto$ `RankinSelberg.sPartIntegral K S` (for the pins above, the standard additive character, the pair $(x,x)$, the section $\varphi(s)$, and the parameters $w,e_1,e_2$) is analytic on a neighbourhood of every point of the half-plane $\{s:a<\mathrm{Re}\,s\}$. Here `sPartIntegral` is the integral, over those classes $q$ in the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ by `rationalCentreUnipotent K` whose chosen representative $q.\mathrm{out}$ lies in `shellZeroOutside K S` (i.e. satisfies $v(\det g)=\max(v(g_{10,v}),v(g_{11,v}))^{2}$ at every finite place $v\notin S$), of the integrand
--   $$\mathbf{1}_{\{\|\det g\|\in[e_1,e_2]\}}(g)\;W(x)(g)\,\overline{W(x)(g)}\;\varphi(s)(g)\;\|\det g\|^{-w},$$
--   against `rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure K`.
--
--   Thirdly, for every real $\sigma>a$ the value of that same $S$-part integral at $\varphi(\sigma)$ has vanishing imaginary part and strictly positive real part.
--
--   This is the bad-place and archimedean half of the test-data theorem for the diagonal Rankin–Selberg integral on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a number field: once the Euler factors outside $S$ have been separated off, what remains is the torus-and-maximal-compact integral treated here, and the assertion is its absolute convergence, its holomorphic continuation to a half-plane reaching past $\mathrm{Re}\,s=1/2$, and its positivity at real points. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.exists_testData_sPartIntegral_self_analyticOnNhd_re_pos`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.exists_testData_sPartIntegral_self_analyticOnNhd_re_pos), which produces the test data realising a non-vanishing Rankin–Selberg integral.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_RankinSelberg_analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_and_pos_of_shell_surgery.lean

import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_RankinSelbergQuotientIntegral
import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_ProductionPinsGeneral
import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_AdelicMaximalCompact
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure
